<!-- The Halo 3-style pre-game lobby (Menu style Halo 3): it stands for the Xbox's ENLISTED PLAYERS
screen (connected\pregame\connected_pregame_screen), the lobby of a network game - co-op hosted
from the campaign lobby (the waiting screen) and a multiplayer game, hosted or joined - and runs
what it ran, the game's own functions under its own buttons: as it opens "net server accept conx"
and "net server allow start", each frame "net splitscreen prejoin players" (the players who joined
on SELECT PROFILE added to the game); Cross "net game speed start" and "net game join player",
START the same, Square "net game delay start" (in the waiting screen of co-op hosted online, the
game made public or private: coop_menu.c), left and right "swap player team", Circle and Back
"net game unjoin player" (the last of this machine's players leaves the game; the co-op host's
cancels it). Laid out as Halo 3's lobby: the column at the left with what is played - the
mission's picture, its name and difficulty (co-op) or the map's picture, the game type on the map
- how the game is reached, its code large, public or private and what Square does; the players at
the right, each in their colour with their team, the host's and this machine's marked (menu_functions.c
"port h3 pregame"). The pictures and emblems are ui.map's own; the rest this folder's art. -->
